    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_baf80011b2db72597a0ad987b2525dd7e08bdbdf95a94a25bf97b839e81c7137",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "In both cited explicit-formula settings the test function is co-designed with the theorem, but by different mechanisms. Twist-family rank bounds require compact support, transform decay, reflection, and strip positivity assembled by convolution; low-zero bounds require a nonnegative band-limited probe adapted to a nonconstant symmetry kernel, leading to a Fredholm extremal problem and sharper proportions.",
